  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="kire-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">כירי</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">kyry</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">kire</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="kire-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>pleasure, happiness</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>χαῖρε, χάιρις</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>והנה מן היאור עולות וגו' בשעה שהשנים יפות הבריות נעשים אחים אילו לאילו, ותרענה באחו אהבה ואחוה בעולם, וכן הוא א' ירעה מקנך ביום ההוא כר נרחב 
                     <app>
                        <lem>כירי כירי</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1 Ox2">כירי קירי</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V">כירי עבד קירי אדון</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">כירי עבד כירי אדון פירוש כלומ' מראין עצמן כאדונים מתגברין על רבם</rdg>
                     </app> מרובה בעולם</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">89,4</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">III 1091: 2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>And, behold, there came up out of the river ... (Gen 41,2) In the years of prosperity men become brothers: And they fed in the Ahu means, love and brotherliness (aḥawah) reigned in the world. In the same strain we read: In that day shall thy cattle feed in large (kar) pastures (Jes 30,23), which means, [when thy cattle feed and there is plenty], pleasure, pleasure greatly in the world. [Freedman / Simon II 822]</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 147 [47c: 28]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">כירי עבד קירי אדון</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>This interpretation also in <bibl type="modern">AC IV 312a</bibl>, <bibl type="modern">Levy II 324ab</bibl>. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 636b</bibl>: Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">χαῖρε</term> imp. of Gr. <term xml:lang="jpa">χαίρω</term> meaning: “’hail!’ ‘hail!’ is largely heard in the world (this meaning is found in <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 287a</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">כירי</term> III and IV). The alternative reading <term xml:lang="jpa">כירי עבד כירי אדון</term> is probably a gloss (mis)interpreting the original reading as <term xml:lang="jpa">כירי</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">χείριος</term> “slave”, <term xml:lang="jpa">קירי</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">qyry</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">κύριος</term> “lord”. See also <bibl type="modern">Shoval-Dudai 94b</bibl>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Shoval-Dudai</title>
                  <citedRange>94β</citedRange>
               </bibl>
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>286b-287a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
